===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/əˈnoʊə/|a=GA}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-anoa.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Either of two related species of small [[Indonesian]] [[water buffalo]] similar in appearance to [[deer]]; {{taxlink|Bubalus quarlesi|species}} or {{taxlink|Bubalus depressicornis|species}}.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1998|author=Jane Whitten|title=Tropical Wildlife of Southeast Asia
|url=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=psuWpwZuX_oC&pg=PA16&dq=%22anoa%22%7C%22anoas%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=NfwOUrTNMOvtiAeLzYDgCg&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22anoa%22%7C%22anoas%22&f=false|page=16
|passage='''Anoas''' need undisturbed forest and cannot adapt to logged areas. The bad-tempered '''anoa''' with its sharp short horns is greatly feared, but in spite of this it is periodically suggested as a potential domestic animal. Anyone who has met with an '''anoa''' ridicules this idea.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2000|author=Michael Alvard|chapter=The Impact of Traditional Subsistence Hunting and Trapping on Prey Populations: Data from Wana Horticuluralists of Upland Central Sulwesi, Indonesia|editors=John G. Robinson; Elizabeth L. Bennett|title=Hunting for Sustainability in Tropical Forests|pageurl=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=ZawmOh3IZ_IC&pg=PA223&dq=%22anoa%22%7C%22anoas%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=NfwOUrTNMOvtiAeLzYDgCg&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22anoa%22%7C%22anoas%22&f=false|page=223
|passage=The Celebes pig and, to a lesser degree, the anoa were the focus of the Wana's large game interests.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2011|author=Colin Groves; Peter Grubb|title=Ungulate Taxonomy|pageurl=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=XAX0bqw-I2oC&pg=PT168&dq=%22anoa%22%7C%22anoas%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=NfwOUrTNMOvtiAeLzYDgCg&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22anoa%22%7C%22anoas%22&f=false|page=unnumbered
|passage=They reported seeing mountain '''anoa''' trophies for sale, and also a living captive animal, in the Toraja highlands; probable lowland '''anoas''' in the Gunung Tangkoko National Park on the N tip of Sulawesi, and evidence of both kinds of '''anoas''' in or near the Dumoga-Bone National Park.}}

====Usage notes====
The two species may constitute a subgenus of {{taxfmt|Bubalus|genus}}. See {{pedia}}

